
# Task 18: Numerical Solution of ODEs Using SciPy

## 1. Objective
The aim is to solve an ordinary differential equation numerically using SciPy.

## 2. Inputs
The differential equation is:

dy/dt = -2y

Initial value: y(0) = 1.

Time interval: 0 to 2.

## 3. Mathematical Operations
The program uses SciPy's solve_ivp() function to approximate the solution of the differential equation over the given time interval.

## 4. Original Output
Initial value = 1.

Estimated value at t = 2 = 0.018355.

## 5. Modified Input
The initial value was changed from 1 to 2.

## 6. Observation
Changing the initial value changes the numerical solution.

## 7. Interpretation
SciPy solves differential equations numerically using an equation and an initial condition.

## 8. Related Real-World Problem
Numerical ODE solvers are used in physics, engineering, population modelling and scientific simulations.

## 9. Assumptions
The differential equation is well-defined over the selected time interval, and the initial value is known.

## 10. New Input Data
The modified initial value is 2.

The differential equation and time interval remain unchanged.

## 11. Output
New initial value = 2.

Estimated value at t = 2 = 0.03671.

## 12. Interpretation of the Modified Problem
Increasing the initial value from 1 to 2 approximately doubles the solution at the same time, demonstrating how initial conditions affect numerical solutions.
